# Quality & Testing

- Use strong typing: TypeScript on the frontend, Python type hints + Pydantic models on the
  backend.
- Validate all external input at the boundary (API requests, retailer feed payloads).
- Use structured (JSON) logging; do not leave ad-hoc `print`/`console.log` debugging in place.
- Every deployable service must expose a health check once it exists.
- Network calls (retailer APIs/feeds, internal services) must use explicit timeouts and retries
  with backoff — never unbounded blocking calls.
- New business logic must be accompanied by new or updated unit/integration tests in the same
  change.
- After implementing a change, run the relevant test suite for the affected area before
  considering the task done. If tests cannot be run (e.g. missing environment), state that
  explicitly rather than silently skipping verification.
- At the end of a task, report: files created, files modified, tests executed (and their
  results), and any remaining issues or known gaps. This reporting is required, not optional.
